{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>To know what is in your heart.</b> This means 'to make known'; and likewise (Exodus 31:13) לדעת כי אני ה׳ מקדשכם — 'to know that I am HaShem who sanctifies you' — said in the commandment of the Sabbath; and the intent in both of them is to make it known to the nations, and so that it become publicized that worship is the essential purpose of the creation of the world." "<b>And it is possible</b> to say concerning the word וירעיבך ('and He made you hungry') that it comes to teach about the perfection of the manna and its excellence: that all who eat it grasp intelligibilia concerning perfection, and this is impossible except after the cessation of the impurity of physical nourishment; as they expounded concerning Moses our master, peace be upon him, in the first chapter of Yoma (Exodus 24:16): ״וכסהו הענן ששת ימים״ — 'and the cloud covered him six days' — why six days? In order to purge the food and drink that was in his bowels. And so here, וירעיבך — in order that the impurity of physical nourishment be consumed from them, and their nourishment was the unleavened cakes (חררה) which they brought out of Egypt; and then their bodies would be renewed by the nourishment of the manna, which is an emanation of the supernal light (אור), and they would be fit to receive the intelligibilia and to cleave to the Shekhinah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "Source cites '(שם כד)' and '(שם לא)'; the former refers to Exodus 24:16 and the latter to Exodus 31:13, following the sequence of prior citations in the commentary. 'תולדת האור' rendered 'an emanation of the supernal light' literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:46.906957967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}